  "docText": [
    "SOLAR®",
    "Biamp Design System",
    "1.0",
    "Badge",
    "Description",
    "Communicates status, category, or a count at a glance. Use for labelling items with semantic meaning — success, warning, danger, info, or neutral. Not for actions (use Button) or navigation (use Link).",
    "Sub-components",
    "badge-dot         6×6 status indicator. Used inside badge pill or standalone.\nbadge-value      Numeric counter pill (20px). Shows selected + danger states.\nbadge-trend      Directional indicator (20×20). Incline, Decline, or Neutral.\nbadge-group     Full-width banner. Badge + message text + chevron action.",
    "Status",
    "Each status maps to a feedback color pair — tinted background + saturated text/border.\nsuccess (green), warning (orange), danger (red), info (turquoise), offline/neutral (gray).",
    "Types",
    "pill              Default. Dot + label in a rounded pill. Read-only.\ntag               Label + close icon. Removable by user.\nicon             Icon-only badge (24×24). Compact action trigger.\nuser             Avatar + label. Identifies a person with status context.",
    "Content",
    "Labels should be 1–2 words: \"Active\", \"Pending\", \"3 errors\". Use sentence case.\nFont is Inter Semi Bold 12px across all badge types.\nBadge-value uses a centered number; keep it short (max 3 digits, then \"99+\").",
    "Rules",
    "DO   Use semantic status colors consistently\nDO   Keep label text under 2 words\nDO   Use badge-group for actionable status banners\nDO   Pair badge-dot with text labels for accessibility",
    "DON'T   Use badge as a button — it's non-interactive (except tag)\nDON'T   Mix status colors in one badge\nDON'T   Use color as the sole indicator — always include text\nDON'T   Exceed \"99+\" in badge-value counters"
  ],
  "pageContext": null
